---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon/Icon.astro';
import '../../components/Directory/directory.css';
import { universities } from '../../lib/directory/data';
---
<Layout title="About the Graduate Supervisor Directory — Atishaya Maharjan" description="Coverage, evidence, funding labels, collection, and portrait approval for the Canadian CS and mathematics graduate supervisor directory.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-8 pb-16">
    <a href="/grad-directory" class="directory-link inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm"><Icon name="arrow-left" /> Back to the directory</a>
    <header class="mt-6">
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-300">A note on the sources</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-medium text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mt-2">About this directory</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">Finding a graduate supervisor often means reading department listings, personal pages, and lab websites one at a time. This resource brings those public signals together, with the original evidence close at hand.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="mt-6 py-6 border-t border-b border-rule dark:border-rule-dark">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Coverage is growing</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">The first pilot covers selected computer science and mathematics faculty at six Canadian universities. A listed professor’s eligibility to supervise a particular program must be confirmed with that program. Inclusion does not imply a university’s endorsement or complete department coverage.</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm">
        {universities.map(u => (
          <li>
            <p><strong>{u.university.name}</strong> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-300">{u.professors.length} records</span></p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-300">{u.coverage}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="py-6 border-b border-rule dark:border-rule-dark">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Read the labels carefully</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-bold">Advertised opening</dt>
          <dd>A source explicitly describes recruiting graduate students or an available position. The openings-only filter excludes past advertised intakes, expired deadlines, conflicting records, and claims whose source checks are overdue.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-bold">General invitation</dt>
          <dd>A standing invitation to prospective students; it does not establish a specific available position.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-bold">Explicitly closed</dt>
          <dd>A source explicitly says the professor is not accepting students, with the stated degree and intake restrictions preserved.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-bold">Availability unknown</dt>
          <dd>No clear statement has been catalogued. Missing information is never interpreted as a rejection.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>
    <section class="py-6 border-b border-rule dark:border-rule-dark">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Funding is a separate question</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">Position funding, a departmental funding policy, and a requirement to bring external funding are recorded separately. A professor holding a grant does not establish an available funded place. Check the original source for amounts, tuition, duration, eligibility, and conditions.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-6 border-b border-rule dark:border-rule-dark">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Collection and freshness</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">A scheduled collector reads public institutional profiles and linked personal or lab pages, including English and French sources. Codex proposes structured records; updates are reviewed before publication. Each claim links to its supporting passage.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">“Checked” is the date a source was successfully read, not confirmation from the professor. An unchanged or undated page may itself be out of date. Source checks become overdue after 90 days. Failed checks preserve the prior evidence rather than changing availability to closed.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">Keyword matching supports names and research interests. Degree and intake filters include only explicitly catalogued information, so they can hide relevant professors whose details are unknown. All dates are interpreted using America/Winnipeg where a timezone is needed.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-6 border-b border-rule dark:border-rule-dark">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Portraits are approved separately</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">Images are proposed from named institutional profiles or linked individual personal/lab profiles. Each exact image must be manually approved against the professor’s identity and affiliation. Approved files are stored locally, and replacements require a new approval. When a match is uncertain or pending, we show initials.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="pt-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Corrections are welcome</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">Use “Report a correction” on a professor’s page, or <a class="directory-link" href="mailto:atishaya7777@gmail.com?subject=Graduate%20directory%20correction">email Atishaya</a>. Include the relevant source link. Please confirm application procedures and availability through the original sources before applying.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
